.TH tix-config 1  "config " 
.SH NAME
tix\-config \- Manage the global tix config
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtix config\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the global tix config
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to the global config file (overrides TIX_CONFIG_PATH and the platform default)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output format for commands that support it (also forwarded to plugins as \-\-tix\-output)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
toml
.IP \(bu 2
default
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Set the log level to trace (shorthand for \-\-log\-level trace)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Set the log level to warn (shorthand for \-\-log\-level warn)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tix\-config\-get(1)
Read a value from the `[cli]` section
.TP
tix\-config\-init(1)
Create the global config interactively
.TP
tix\-config\-set(1)
Set a value in the `[cli]` section
.TP
tix\-config\-show(1)
Print the global config document
.TP
tix\-config\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
